# Refreshed 2026-06-20 at v6.2.33 — AGNOS stdlib syscall-ABI pack. Added 1
# gotcha (gotchas.cyml): `CYRIUS_ARCH_X86` is predefined on EVERY x86 build,
# agnos included, so an arch-macro-only-guarded stdlib file silently takes the
# Linux syscall branch on the agnos target (sakshi log corruption, compiles
# clean) — the agnos branch must `#ifdef CYRIUS_TARGET_AGNOS` first; nested
# `#ifdef` works, `#else` does not. Theme: agnos codegen is self-host-invisible,
# so per-target syscall selection needs a real `CYRIUS_TARGET_AGNOS=1` build +
# emit-inspect, never just self-host.
#
# Refreshed 2026-06-18 at v6.2.22 — Phase-0 growable-region foundation
# (fixup_tbl / fn-tables / codebuf migrated from fixed caps to grow-on-demand).
# Added 2 gotchas (gotchas.cyml): the grow/rehash/relocation paths are
# SELF-HOST-INVISIBLE (cycc stays under every cap, so only a forced-grow test
# catches relocation/rehash bugs); and the migration mechanics (codebuf
# re-derive-from-base relocation safety + disp32-RMW guard band; the 8192 fn-cap
# was a magic literal scattered across 6 subsystems, colliding textually with 5
# unrelated 8192-capped tables → surgical per-context swaps, not a global replace).
# Theme: "byte-identical self-host" proves only the no-grow path; a cold grow
# path needs its own forced test or it ships broken to the first consumer past the cap.
